{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nToday `rebar bridge` exposes `{preview,sync,pause,resume}`. No `bridge status` subcommand exists, and the earlier top...\nThe current production canary queries GitHub Actions for heartbeat state. Reconciler health also has two overlapping ...\n## Durable state and writer contract\nConsolidate the two pass-record producers into one. A mutating reconciler pass writes minimal JSON truth to the Git o...\nUpdate the ref with observed-OID compare-and-swap using `--force-with-lease=refs/reconciler/last-pass:<observed-oid>`...\nFinalization advances `refs/reconciler/last-pass` before releasing `refs/reconciler/lock`. Keep the lock heartbeat ac...\nRich detail is one fixed rolling file, `.tickets-tracker/.bridge_state/last-pass.json`, overwritten rather than accum...\nRemove duplicate producers plus dead `pre_fsck`, `post_fsck`, and `capture_baseline` data. Update every caller and as...\n## Environment identity\nThis identity rule is scoped only to the new last-pass writer and status target; it does not modify inbound event met...\n## Status snapshot and exact contract\n`bridge status` is a fast, read-only, non-mutating single snapshot. Add its parser, metavar, help, and dispatch in `s...\nStatus never calls `steal()` and never sleeps for a lease. It reads the authoritative last-pass ref, optional matchin...\nText and structured output expose the same verdict and facts. Co-occurring conditions resolve by total precedence `PA...\n- `HEALTHY`, matching successful last-pass record, exit 0.\n- `PAUSED`, matching state while intentionally paused, exit 0 even when old; pause takes precedence over age failure.\n- `RUNNING`, lock currently held in this single snapshot, exit 0 and include lock OID, fence, and lease.\n- `STALE`, matching non-paused record older than an explicitly supplied `--max-age`, exit 1.\n- Omitting `--max-age` disables age failure; there is no implicit threshold.\n- `FOREIGN`, durable record environment differs from the explicitly selected target, exit 1 with both ids.\n- `NEVER_RUN`, no durable last-pass record and no live lock, exit 1. The compatibility spelling preserves the former ...\n- `FAILED`, last-pass records a process-surviving hard failure, exit 1 with `failure_kind`.\n- `CRASHED` is not inferred by one status invocation. It is the canary result when two read-only snapshots separated ...\nThe lock blob is the lease configuration source. The holder carries `lease_secs`; current acquisition defaults to `_r...\nThe two witnesses are deliberately separate. Last-pass records success and failures for which the process can execute...\n## Canary cutover and rollback\nRoll out producer before consumer: retain explicit `REBAR_CANARY_HEARTBEAT_SOURCE=github-api` during bootstrap until ...\nFor one release, retain the GitHub Actions API heartbeat source behind explicit rollback selection `REBAR_CANARY_HEAR...\n## Architecture record and numbering convention\nCreate ADR `0094-reconciler-last-pass-two-witness-status.md` explaining the authoritative last-pass ref, fixed rich-d...\n## Verification plan\nAuthor all behavioral tests RED-first under held-out TDD. The happy path proves a matching durable success. Held-out ...\n- canonical and legacy command parity for options, text/JSON, schema, errors, exits, hidden legacy help, and no mutat...\n- `HEALTHY`, `PAUSED`, `RUNNING`, `STALE`, `FOREIGN`, `NEVER_RUN`, `FAILED`, and canary `CRASHED` contracts;\n- omitted `--max-age` disables age failure and paused remains exit 0;\n- local last-pass identity cannot masquerade as `reconciler`, while inbound legacy Jira identity and workflow default...\n- hard process-surviving failure pushes minimal durable state before lock release even when workflow commit-back is s...\n- SIGKILL/OOM is represented only by stalled fence and two-snapshot lease classification;\n- last-pass CAS contention follows the exact three-attempt backoff and persistent ref push failure fails loudly witho...\n... (18 lines truncated)\n[full output: \"$HOME/Library/Application Support/rtk/tee/1786328124_jq_-r__description___gsub______________x.log\"]"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786328125006647001,"uuid":"7cd17c25-33a1-43ea-837a-5f7a47a83a70"}